+stops at the `]` of the attribute selector *inside* it. It now walks the source
+with a quote-aware scanner. Whatever replaces it, prove it by reintroducing a
+known-bad selector and watching the check fail — a green run means nothing until
+you have seen it go red.
+
+**`page.url()` is synchronous.** It returns a string, not a promise. `.catch()`
+on it throws, and inside a best-effort helper that swallows its own errors the
+whole capture disappears with no sign anything went wrong.
 
