+### Failure forensics
+
+Every connector failure writes a capture: full-page screenshot, page HTML, final
+URL and title, under `CONNECTOR_FORENSICS_DIR` (`/app/forensics`, its own volume;
+newest 50 kept). A summary also goes into `SyncLog.metadata.forensics` and the
+log stream, so the URL and error are reachable without shell access to the
+container. Credentials the connector holds are stripped from the HTML first.
+`CONNECTOR_FORENSICS=off` disables it.
+
+The final URL is the field to read first: a redirect back to `/login` means the
+session died, which is indistinguishable from a missing selector at the call
+site.
+
+`ConnectorService` captures inside the `catch`, deliberately **before** the
+`finally` that closes the browser. Move the call after `close()` and there is no
+page left to photograph.
+
 ### Known broken, with evidence
 
-- **Six selectors are invalid CSS.** `button:contains("Add")` is jQuery syntax;
-  `querySelectorAll` throws `SyntaxError`. Confirmed in real Chromium. They sit
-  in the availability paths of Filmmakers, CastingNetwork, JobWork and Wanted,
-  and fail regardless of what the sites look like.
+- **The six invalid selectors are fixed.** They were jQuery
+  (`button:contains("Add")`), which made the whole selector string invalid CSS,
+  so the valid alternatives beside them never ran either. They now go through
+  `findByCssOrText`: structural selector first, button label as fallback.
+  `npm run check:selectors` walks all 70 selectors through real Chromium and
+  exits non-zero on any that are not valid CSS.
+- **Fixing them removed two false-success paths.** JobWork and Wanted wrapped
+  the add-availability button in `if (addButton)` and Wanted's profile submit in
+  a `try` commented "form might auto-save". Both reported success without having
+  clicked anything. They now throw `PlatformChangedError`.
 - **e-TALENTA and Schauspielervideos have zero selectors.** They are API
   adapters against APIs the project has no access to. They cannot work as
   written.
-- **No connector has ever run against a live platform.** Deeper selectors
-  (`.upload-success`, `textarea[name="biography"]`, `[data-action="add-availability"]`)
-  are speculative. Login selectors are valid CSS and plausible; everything past
-  login probably is not.
